# Changelog
All notable changes to gVirtualXray will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), and this project adheres
to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).

## [Unreleased]

### Added
- TBA

### Changed
- TBA

### Fixed
- TBA

## [2.1.0] - 2026-06-09

### Added
- OpenMP backend on CPU (it's slow, but it is a possible solution when a GPU is not available).
- Compute the peak signal-noise ratio (PSNR) over a given number of rotations around the sample.
- Can query the GPU to retrieve the largest possible number of energy bin in the spectrum.
- Can query the GPU to retrieve the largest possible number of pixels of the detector.
- Make it possible to resize the detector: the pixel pitch is adjusted, whist the number of pixels remain the same.
- Expose the generation of iso-surfaces using the Marching Cubes algorithm.
- Compute the pixel size in radiograph (taken in the middle of the sample bounding box).
- Generate a report to show the size of the sample on the detector. It can be useful to assess the theoretical
  visibility of defects.
- Integration of two digital twins (Python only), the DTHE at INSA Lyon, and the DIAD beamline at
  the Diamond Light Source.
- Can retrieve the total incident energy without the energy response of the detector.
- Integration with Numpy (computeXRayImage and makeIsoSurface).
- Can set the number of photons per cm2 at one metre.
- Integrate https://github.com/kylechampley/XrayPhysics to generate X-ray tube spectra.
- Filter the spectra using xraylib.
- Use of mixed-precision floating point numbers.
- Compute the optimal source-object distance for a given cone-beam geometry.
- Move the sample by adjusting the source-object distance for a given cone-beam geometry.
- Add the detector gain to emulate under and overexposure.
- Make it possible to save the images in unsigned short, either with gain applied, or white level after
  flat-field correction.
- Can compute the source-detector distance, the object-detector distance and the source-object distance.
- Make it possible to detect the lack of OpenGL and create one automatically using createOpenGLContext().
- Make it possible to choose the CPU architecture (aarch64 or x86_64) to build Python wheels with Manylinux 2.34.
- Add a functionality in gvxr-core and SimpleGVXR to handle inherent filters.
- Can compute the effective atomic numbers of heterogeneous materials.
- Can save STL file in either binary (default in SimpleGVXR) or ASCII formats.
- Add accessors to FOV, magnification, SOD, SDD, and ODD.

### Changed
- In the core API, the method Mixture::getWeightSet() is renamed Mixture::getMassWeightSet.
- Make it possible to set the inherent filtration in the functions as follows:
    - gvxrPython3.utils.getSpectrumSpekpy
    - gvxrPython3.utils.getSpekpySpectrum
    - gvxrPython3.utils.getSpectrumXpecgen
    - gvxrPython3.utils.getXpecgenSpectrum
    - gvxrPython3.utils.loadSpectrumSpekpy
    - gvxrPython3.utils.loadSpectrumXpecgen
    - gvxrPython3.utils.loadSpekpySpectrum
    - gvxrPython3.utils.loadXpecgenSpectrum
  The default values are: 0.5 mm of Al.

### Fixed
- Ray tracing on CPU now works.
- gauss2d has a signed/unsigned int issue.
- Make sure the unit of length is applied when creating a mesh with makeIsoSurface.

## [2.0.10] - 2025-02-17

### Added
- Print out some of the compilation parameters that can be turned on/off
- Can interactively change the markers' size in the 3D visualisation
- Make it possible to set a mixture using symbols for the chemical elements and make the weight of one of the elements the balance of the others.
- Ignore energy bins that do not contribute to the spectrum.

## [2.0.9] - 2025-02-06

### Fixed
- All the functions of SimpleGVXR are documented using Doxygen and are available in Python.

## [2.0.8] - 2024-08-01

### Added
- Rotation of the source centre on its focal spot or any arbitrary rotation centre.
- Show the 1st pixel position in the 3D visualisation.
- Show the detector centre in the 3D visualisation.
- Show the world's origin.
- Can tilt the detector.
- Rotation axis for CT scan acquisition can be overwritten.
- Exporter to JSON file (Python only)
- Add new scintillators: Gd2O2S DRZ-Plus, NaI, and others from https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nima.2015.08.041.
- There is a new function (`getSupportedScintillatorMaterials`) to find which scintillator materials are supported.
- There is now a function to perform a CT scan in C++. It makes it possible to save the CT scan acquisition parameters in a JSON file.
- It is now possible to hide a window.
- It is now possible to use the close window widget (i.e. clicking on cross at top of the window).
- Add an interface in SimpleGVXR to the implicit modelling functionalities. It is now possible to create virtual samples using metaballs.
- Can now invert face normals (it was previously restricted to vertex normals).
- When the marching cubes is used to create a surface from a 3D volume made of voxels, the volume is padded first to ascertain the surface is closed.
- Add new phantoms:
    - Added a step wedge phantom that a user can tweak (e.g. number of steps, width, height, etc.)
    - Make it possible to create a phantom made of a cylinder with sphere inserts.
    - It is possible to create a cuboid that corresponds to some kind of foam.
- Can use the `loadMeshFile` function and set the parent. It is useful when adding one mesh into another one. This way, if the parent is moved, the children follow.
- Can move a visualisation window from the code.

## [2.0.7] - 2023-11-08

### Added
- Can create cuboids. It's simpler for the user than a cube that is rescaled.
- The smallest total energy for a bin is 1 eV instead of 0.
- Can now set the X-ray tube voltage to generate a beam spectrum. The method is not enabled, tho.
- The focal spot can be a square shape.
- The focal spot can be a square rectangle.
- It is now possible to have a detector that is not perpendicular to the vector from the source to the centre of the detector.

## [2.0.6] - 2023-05-23

### Added
- Add Poisson noise
- Can generate flat field images, with and without Poisson noise
- Can set the total number of photons. This is useful when using a complex polychromatic spectrum with Poisson noise.
- Enable the use of software rendering using Mesa.
- Support spectral imaging.

## [2.0.5] - 2023-03-08

### Fixed
- Both versions 2.0.4 & 2.0.5 are the same due to mishandling on pypi.

## [2.0.4] - 2023-03-08

### Fixed
- Fix bug in loading the spectrum from a text file (JSON)
- Fix bug in converting voxel data in HU to mu. There must have been an infinite loop.

## [2.0.3] - 2023-01-13

### Added
- Add focal spot to json2gvxr.py (Python).
- Add plugins for CIL (Python).
- Create functions to extract the beam spectrum from the JSON file without loading the spectrum (Python).

### Fixed
- When json2gvxr.py is used, file path in json files are relative to the json file, not the python script (Python).

## [2.0.2] - 2022-10-09

### Added
- The plan is to use 2.0.2 for the training at IBSim-4i 2022.
- Can assess the topology of meshes.
- Add the detector impulse response (as a LSF).

### Fixed
- Broadcast the C++ exceptions (throw) to Python (except).
- Better handling of exiting without explicitly calling destroyAllWindows().
- Better support of EGL.
- Include json2gvxr.py and utils.py in the Python package.

## [2.0.1] - 2022-08-05

### Added
- Add support for GLAD as an alternative to GLEW.

### Removed
- Get rid off all the OpenGL 2.x code.

### Fixed
- Do not link against libpython3 in Manylinux to fix issues with the repaired wheels.
- OpenGL windows are made visible if needed when `renderLoop` is called.

## [2.0.0] - 2022-08-02

### Added
- pip wheels can be build for Linux and Windows.

## [1.1.5] - 2021-07-06

### Fixed
- Move the OpenGL creation into gvxr-core
- Make sure it compiles on MS Window, Mac OS X, and GNU/Linux (desktop & supercomputer)

## [1.1.4] - 2020-09-08

### Fixed
- Now fully support EGL context
- Compiles on SuperComputing Wales
- Successful run of unit tests on SuperComputing Wales

## [1.1.3] - 2020-09-03

### Added
- Can load meshes from RAM

### Fixed
- Improve Numpy support
- See log for further bug fixes

